  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded 3.3% a year from $65.1 billion in FY2017 to $87.0 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F201]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step change rather than a straight line: revenue rose 4.8% in FY2020 and 7.3% in FY2021, then slowed to 2.3% in FY2023 and 0.3% in FY2025 [D147][D198][D302][D406]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2020's 4.8% growth came on a 4% unit volume increase, with high single-digit volume in North America and pantry loading from the COVID-19 pandemic [D147][P72]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2019 operating margin fell 11.9pp to 8.1% on an $8.3 billion impairment charge for Shave Care goodwill and the Gillette intangible [D109][F23][P62]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Excluding that charge, operating margin has held between 20.0% and 24.3% every year, and FY2026's 22.7% sits just above the 22.1% window median [F22][F29][F30][D648]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The US was the growth engine: its share of revenue rose from 40.8% in FY2018 to 47.9% in FY2026 [D512][D534]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2026 the US contributed just 0.1pp of the 3.3% growth while non-US contributed 3.1pp, as non-US sales grew 6.1% [D536][D457][D511][D510]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 net sales rose 3% on favorable foreign exchange of 2% and pricing of 1%, with unit volume and mix unchanged [P26]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Fabric & Home Care is the largest segment at 34.8% of revenue and added 0.8pp in FY2026, while Beauty added 1.3pp on 7.1% growth [D541][D543][D603][D602]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 4.1% a year against 3.3% revenue growth, but FY2026 operating income fell 3.4% while revenue rose 3.3% [F202][F201][D458][D457]."}
  ]},
