    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $19.6 billion was 1.22x net income in FY2026, above the 1.02x window median, and free cash flow of $15.1 billion was 0.94x [F80][F40][D444][D660][F100][D445]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin of 17.4% sits between the 14.4% window low and 20.5% high [D441][D652][D653]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating cash flow rose 10% as inventories consumed $641 million for safety stock and new products, partly offset by $919 million from higher payables [P3][D462]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex rose 16.9% to $4.4 billion, or 5.1% of revenue, and capex ran 1.40x D&A, the highest ratio in the window [D464][F90][D440][D446]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt was $24.2 billion, or 27.8% of revenue, better than the -1.0% staples peer median but only the 33rd percentile of six peers [D450][D451][D677][D676]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio of 0.68x is below the 0.72x window median and near the 0.63x low, with working capital at -$12.5 billion [F180][D663][D661][F170]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $5.0 billion plus dividends of $10.2 billion were 100.7% of free cash flow, and the diluted share count fell 1.3% [X134][X144][D453][D476]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Long-term debt fell 8.6% to $22.8 billion while the current portion rose to $6.5 billion [F190][D468][X194]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
